 When studying the Mirt package and  using the new 8.0 version, as LogLik of the unidimensional model comparing to Itm's LogLik, they do not show the same results. I got some doubts regarding my results.
As the LogLik are diferent, I observed that the program still doing the interaction and the LogLik stops before ending the interactions. I would like to make it clear that this does not occur when we calculate it using the unidimensional model com
few interactions, as for example the LTSAT, but for the SAT12 example and for the data set that I'm working with the LogLik values are diferent, as the following script.

data(SAT12)
SAT12
